    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly, natural wind isn't going to follow a rhythmic, timed pulse every 15 minutes on the dot. it's too precise for that. plus, why is it only coming from the direction of the municipal offices? if it were just wind, it would be happening all over the district. it feels like they're testing the efficacy of a \"passive compliance\" system here. given how these frequencies can bypass conscious awareness and hit the nervous system directly, what would be the strategic advantage for a local government to deploy this kind of acoustic tech at these specific decibel levels?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
